WEBVTT

00:01.460 --> 00:03.500
<b>BUNKYU YEAR 2 (1862)</b>

00:02.500 --> 00:06.670
<b>Say, darling. You were summoned
by Lord Yasuhide yesterday, weren't you?</b>

00:07.080 --> 00:08.880
<b>What did you two talk about?</b>

00:08.880 --> 00:14.130
<b>Well, get this. Lord Yasuhide
prepared a sword especially for me.</b>

00:14.380 --> 00:15.630
<b>Oh really?</b>

00:15.630 --> 00:18.710
<b>Seems he's been impressed with my work lately.</b>

00:19.210 --> 00:23.460
<b>He said: "The dedication that you've shown
in your daily service is deserving of reward."</b>

00:23.460 --> 00:25.460
<b>I could hardly believe my ears!</b>

00:25.880 --> 00:27.580
<b>How amazing!</b>

00:31.170 --> 00:32.040
<b>Whaddya think?</b>

00:32.330 --> 00:33.830
<b>Oh wow.</b>

00:33.830 --> 00:36.880
<b>I went and picked it up
from a sword shop called Tamagawa.</b>

00:36.880 --> 00:38.710
<b>What a superb katana.</b>

00:39.290 --> 00:40.500
<b>I know, right?</b>

02:12.290 --> 02:15.380
<b>A cursed blade forged by a blacksmith
who married a demon?</b>

02:15.880 --> 02:22.170
<b>Yes. I know this is slightly outside the range of work
you normally deal with, but I thought I would mention it.</b>

02:22.500 --> 02:23.290
<b>Interesting.</b>

02:27.040 --> 02:30.380
<b>In this light, you two look like a happily married couple.</b>

02:31.790 --> 02:35.630
<b>Oh, stop it, Miura-sama. Don't tease me like that.</b>

02:36.080 --> 02:38.750
<b>Speaking of wives, is yours doing well?</b>

02:39.130 --> 02:43.210
<b>You mean Kinu? She is.
You should come pay us a visit sometime.</b>

02:43.330 --> 02:44.710
<b>I'm sure she'd love it.</b>

02:45.210 --> 02:48.630
<b>I find it hard to believe
she'd ever be happy to see my face.</b>

02:49.210 --> 02:51.250
<b>Well, just take my word for it.</b>

02:52.040 --> 02:55.330
<b>Tell me, do you have any interest
in raising a family yourself?</b>

02:55.630 --> 02:56.670
<b>Not particularly.</b>

02:56.790 --> 02:59.960
<b>Shucks, Naotsugu-sama is really
asking the important questions!</b>

03:00.170 --> 03:01.130
<b>Right, Ofuu?</b>

03:01.420 --> 03:03.670
<b>Jeez! Don't even start, Dad.</b>

03:03.830 --> 03:06.250
<b>Look, the dishes are piling up.</b>

03:06.880 --> 03:09.540
<b>So, back to the subject of that cursed sword...</b>

03:09.710 --> 03:11.130
<b>Oh, right.</b>

03:11.330 --> 03:13.420
<b>A man by the name of Mataroku Sugino,</b>

03:13.420 --> 03:18.420
<b>an aide who serves the Aizu retainer
Lord Hatakeyama at his residence here in Edo,</b>

03:18.420 --> 03:20.130
<b>apparently purchased it three days ago.</b>

03:20.540 --> 03:22.210
<b>How very strange.</b>

03:22.460 --> 03:23.710
<b>What do you mean?</b>

03:23.710 --> 03:26.420
<b>Aides like that only handle odd jobs
around the residence, no?</b>

03:26.880 --> 03:30.830
<b>It doesn't makes sense for someone of such
standing to go out of their way to buy a Kadono blade,</b>

03:30.830 --> 03:32.210
<b>and a cursed one at that.</b>

03:33.170 --> 03:35.630
<b>Actually, there's a good explanation for it.</b>

03:35.790 --> 03:38.290
<b>Are you familiar with the Tosa Loyalist Party?</b>

03:41.000 --> 03:45.790
<b>Last year, a man from Tosa named Zuizan Takechi
gathered warriors from his home town,</b>

03:45.790 --> 03:48.630
<b>and founded the Tosa Loyalist Party.</b>

03:49.290 --> 03:53.580
<b>The shogunate's approach to diplomacy
after the foreign ships arrived a few years back</b>

03:53.580 --> 03:55.080
<b>was dubious even by my standards.</b>

03:55.670 --> 04:00.420
<b>This new party was organized around nativism
in support of the Emperor, however,</b>

04:00.420 --> 04:04.790
<b>they took it a step further by promoting
"collective" loyalty over individual loyalty.</b>

04:05.380 --> 04:08.790
<b>I imagine many more warriors
will join their cause over time.</b>

04:09.670 --> 04:10.880
<b>You're well informed.</b>

04:11.170 --> 04:14.750
<b>Some Tosa retainers live in Edo, you see.</b>

04:14.920 --> 04:17.750
<b>The new era has brought about an ideological shift
and now the majority of people believe</b>

04:17.750 --> 04:21.420
<b>that katana should be wielded in service
to our beliefs and not for the ruling lords.</b>

04:21.960 --> 04:26.170
<b>So, it doesn't surprise me to hear
that people are arming themselves.</b>

04:28.290 --> 04:31.330
<b>I know their methods deviate
from how samurai should act.</b>

04:31.710 --> 04:35.710
<b>Yet seeing these men has given me pause.
Maybe change is for the best.</b>

04:36.290 --> 04:39.540
<b>The shogunate has cast aside their pride as warriors
to bow to foreign powers.</b>

04:39.540 --> 04:41.080
<b>Is serving them the right thing to do?</b>

04:41.080 --> 04:42.290
<b>I'm not sure...</b>

04:43.210 --> 04:45.630
<b>Pardon me. Forget what I just said.</b>

04:46.380 --> 04:48.290
<b>I'm in a similar position.</b>

04:49.080 --> 04:50.920
<b>Really, you, too?</b>

04:51.630 --> 04:56.000
<b>Yes. There are times when I lose sight
of what I'm doing with myself.</b>

04:56.630 --> 04:58.210
<b>Life never goes as you expect.</b>

04:58.710 --> 05:01.000
<b>Yes. Truly.</b>

05:01.750 --> 05:04.880
<b>Anyways, I would like to have a look
at that cursed sword.</b>

05:04.880 --> 05:07.040
<b>Then, let's go see it for ourselves.</b>

05:07.330 --> 05:08.170
<b>Are you sure?</b>

05:09.130 --> 05:12.130
<b>I'm the one who brought it up, after all.</b>

05:18.710 --> 05:21.170
<b>Please forgive our sudden and unannounced visit.</b>

05:21.500 --> 05:24.040
<b>Is there a Mataroku Sugino-dono here?</b>

05:24.960 --> 05:27.420
<b>Uh, Mataroku... you say?</b>

05:28.210 --> 05:30.290
<b>Hm? What's the matter?</b>

05:30.290 --> 05:31.080
<b>Oh!</b>

05:31.290 --> 05:34.080
<b>These gentlemen were just asking to see Mataroku...</b>

05:34.420 --> 05:37.080
<b>My apologies, but Mataroku is gone.</b>

05:38.040 --> 05:39.210
<b>Oh...</b>

05:40.540 --> 05:42.710
<b>Would you happen to know when he might come back?</b>

05:43.080 --> 05:46.130
<b>No. In fact, it's likely that he will never return.</b>

05:46.750 --> 05:49.130
<b>Really? Why is that?</b>

05:49.710 --> 05:54.830
<b>Because just this morning, Mataroku Sugino
murdered his wife and fled from the estate.</b>

05:55.630 --> 05:56.540
<b>Jin-dono!</b>

05:57.040 --> 05:58.420
<b>Seems we were too late.</b>

05:58.710 --> 06:00.040
<b>Let's go search for him.</b>

06:00.040 --> 06:00.750
<b>Right.</b>

06:02.080 --> 06:03.080
<b>Tsuchiura-sama!</b>

06:04.670 --> 06:09.630
<b>Wait. Lord Yasuhide has said he wishes
to meet with you two.</b>

06:14.750 --> 06:17.040
<b>It is a pleasure to meet your acquaintance</b>

06:17.040 --> 06:21.130
<b>My name is Yasuhide Hatakeyama
and I am the lord of this estate.</b>

06:21.960 --> 06:27.920
<b>Sir! I am Naotsugu Miura. I currently serve
as a civil administrator for the shogunate.</b>

06:28.500 --> 06:29.000
<b>And I am...</b>

06:29.000 --> 06:31.170
<b>Jinya-dono, yes?</b>

06:34.040 --> 06:35.380
<b>Be at ease.</b>

06:37.540 --> 06:38.580
<b>Jin-dono!</b>

06:39.040 --> 06:41.960
<b>Please, Hatakeyama-dono. Forgive his transgression.</b>

06:42.210 --> 06:44.580
<b>Oh, it's fine. Think nothing of it.</b>

06:45.080 --> 06:49.420
<b>I've heard talk of the fierce warrior
who has slain countless demons in Edo.</b>

06:50.380 --> 06:53.040
<b>I did not invite Jinya-dono here out of ill-intent.</b>

06:53.420 --> 06:58.380
<b>I wanted to see for myself what a man
with enough superhuman strength</b>

06:58.380 --> 07:01.580
<b>to fell demons with a single blade looks like. That's all.</b>

07:02.170 --> 07:05.670
<b>There are many who meet their ruin
enthralled by the supernatural.</b>

07:05.670 --> 07:09.130
<b>Yet you have slayed various monsters
without succumbing to temptation,</b>

07:09.130 --> 07:12.210
<b>as a true champion of the people should.</b>

07:12.630 --> 07:14.500
<b>I don't need your flattery.</b>

07:14.500 --> 07:17.330
<b>Surely you didn't call me here just to gab about nothing.</b>

07:23.960 --> 07:27.080
<b>You're correct to assume I asked you here for a reason.</b>

07:27.670 --> 07:32.790
<b>I have a proposal, Jinya-dono.
What would you say to formally entering my service?</b>

07:33.080 --> 07:38.130
<b>Although I have been permitted to wield a blade,
I am no more than a commoner by blood.</b>

07:38.420 --> 07:41.420
<b>I would not consider myself worthy
of serving a distinguished samurai clan.</b>

07:42.040 --> 07:47.080
<b>It's fine. This would be a personal contract
between you and me. Your status is of no issue.</b>

07:47.500 --> 07:51.710
<b>As a matter of fact, Tsuchiura here
is man of similar circumstances.</b>

07:54.040 --> 07:56.920
<b>I see. Similar circumstances, eh?</b>

07:58.790 --> 08:02.040
<b>Our country is currently at a crossroads.</b>

08:02.670 --> 08:04.830
<b>Engaging with foreign powers...</b>

08:04.830 --> 08:08.540
<b>They like to put a positive spin on it
by saying they've "opened up" our borders,</b>

08:09.170 --> 08:12.210
<b>but at this rate, Japan is doomed to become a colony.</b>

08:12.750 --> 08:15.000
<b>The feudal system we have will collapse,</b>

08:15.000 --> 08:18.420
<b>bringing an end to the peaceful reign
that Tokugawa has maintained for years</b>

08:18.750 --> 08:21.630
<b>and leaving no need for samurai in the new era.</b>

08:21.920 --> 08:25.130
<b>It's only a matter of time before
they simply cease to exist.</b>

08:25.380 --> 08:27.080
<b>Wait, Hatakeyama-dono! That can't be...</b>

08:27.080 --> 08:30.380
<b>Those in support of ending isolationism
fail to understand this reality!</b>

08:32.630 --> 08:36.170
<b>Although I have already retired from service...</b>

08:36.500 --> 08:43.460
<b>I love this country. I want to uphold the reign
of Tokugawa and the pride of the samurai.</b>

08:43.750 --> 08:47.170
<b>The only way I see that happening
is by ridding us of the barbarians.</b>

08:48.130 --> 08:51.040
<b>And I will use whatever means necessary.</b>

08:52.380 --> 08:55.960
<b>You possess the strength
to wipe out any number of men.</b>

08:56.540 --> 09:00.460
<b>That's why I implore you
to help us protect the status quo.</b>

09:01.830 --> 09:04.710
<b>I appreciate your high opinion of me,
but I'm not a learned man.</b>

09:05.420 --> 09:08.580
<b>Whenever people speak of things like
isolationism or expulsion, I can't help but drone it out.</b>

09:09.250 --> 09:13.750
<b>Oh? So, you have no stake in what becomes of this land?</b>

09:15.040 --> 09:18.500
<b>Years ago, there was a demon
who told me something similar.</b>

09:19.420 --> 09:24.040
<b>About how this country would undergo great change
after being exposed to outside elements and cultures.</b>

09:24.790 --> 09:28.330
<b>Yet demonkind would find itself
unable to keep up with the times,</b>

09:28.540 --> 09:34.040
<b>and eventually become nothing
more than characters spoken of in fairy tales.</b>

09:34.500 --> 09:39.880
<b>Well, I must give that demon credit.
The exact same could be said of us.</b>

09:39.880 --> 09:43.040
<b>Samurai are on the verge
of being lost to the changing times.</b>

09:44.250 --> 09:45.710
<b>All the more reason we need you.</b>

09:47.000 --> 09:49.080
<b>I'm sorry, but I cannot help.</b>

09:51.460 --> 09:56.380
<b>No matter what methods you employ,
I will think no less of you for it.</b>

09:56.540 --> 10:00.880
<b>However, much like you, I am in pursuit of my own goals.</b>

10:02.710 --> 10:06.710
<b>Although mine are merely selfish
and menial when compared to yours.</b>

10:07.420 --> 10:09.330
<b>Still, they mean everything to me.</b>

10:09.670 --> 10:13.460
<b>It doesn't matter who comes begging,
I cannot afford to compromise on how I live at this point.</b>

10:14.380 --> 10:17.250
<b>Besides, it's impractical for me to serve you, regardless.</b>

10:17.460 --> 10:19.080
<b>And why is that?</b>

10:19.330 --> 10:23.540
<b>I can understand the noble sentiment behind
taking up arms in defiance of the changing times.</b>

10:23.670 --> 10:29.630
<b>Therefore, it's only appropriate for your actions to be
what guides the cycle of prosperity and decline.</b>

10:30.710 --> 10:35.630
<b>On the other hand, I haven't even figured out
a clear motivation for wielding my blade.</b>

10:35.960 --> 10:41.130
<b>An irresolute man like me has no right taking part
in battles that will determine the shape of the future.</b>

10:41.670 --> 10:45.710
<b>So you're telling me it has nothing to do with
the ethical implications or any conflicts in ideology,</b>

10:45.710 --> 10:49.170
<b>you can't join our cause because
it doesn't fit with your aesthetic sensibilities?</b>

10:50.210 --> 10:53.210
<b>That's not to say I find any beauty in my own actions.</b>

10:53.750 --> 10:58.630
<b>However, surrendering my will for the sake of bloodshed
is a level of disgrace that I cannot bear.</b>

11:04.790 --> 11:07.920
<b>It seems there's no point in trying to convince you further.</b>

11:08.460 --> 11:12.460
<b>I'm not spurning you or your ideals.
I'm simply pigheaded.</b>

11:13.250 --> 11:15.920
<b>There's no need to debase yourself like that.</b>

11:16.380 --> 11:21.170
<b>For I, too, know what it means to settle
on a course that you cannot stray from.</b>

11:26.000 --> 11:28.460
<b>Naotsugu. We should get going.</b>

11:28.790 --> 11:30.000
<b>That cursed blade is still out there.</b>

11:30.290 --> 11:31.710
<b>Oh, r-right.</b>

11:31.880 --> 11:35.000
<b>Farewell, Hatakeyama-dono. Please excuse us.</b>

11:35.580 --> 11:38.540
<b>If you insist. See them out, Tsuchiura.</b>

11:43.000 --> 11:45.920
<b>Ah, one thing. In regards to Sugino...</b>

11:46.500 --> 11:50.540
<b>My understanding is that he was interested
in visiting a restaurant called Tomizen.</b>

11:51.040 --> 11:54.580
<b>For reasons to do with a Takechi and some Tosa party.</b>

11:55.130 --> 11:58.670
<b>I just hope it hasn't turned into anything ugly.</b>

12:08.750 --> 12:10.330
<b>Tsuchiura-dono, was it?</b>

12:10.750 --> 12:12.580
<b>No need to be formal with me.</b>

12:12.580 --> 12:15.170
<b>Very well. Just Tsuchiura, then.</b>

12:16.210 --> 12:18.330
<b>May I ask why you serve Hatakeyama-dono?</b>

12:19.500 --> 12:21.750
<b>I was once met with betrayal...</b>

12:22.210 --> 12:24.830
<b>Or rather, found myself unable to trust someone.</b>

12:25.670 --> 12:30.170
<b>The person who saved me from the depths of despair
was Lord Yasuhide. He told me:</b>

12:30.630 --> 12:36.290
<b>"Both demons and samurai are on the verge of being
abandoned by the modern age as relics from the past."</b>

12:36.540 --> 12:41.920
<b>"We are compatriots. There is no good reason
that we cannot join forces."</b>

12:42.750 --> 12:45.210
<b>That is why I serve Lord Yasuhide.</b>

12:46.210 --> 12:49.210
<b>I have placed my trust in him.</b>

12:50.130 --> 12:53.630
<b>Seeing as how you live among them,
you must have also realized...</b>

12:54.000 --> 12:56.040
<b>demons are incompatible with humans.</b>

12:57.380 --> 13:02.460
<b>Yet Lord Yasuhide has accepted us.
The significance of that should not be lost on you.</b>

13:03.170 --> 13:04.670
<b>I'm grateful for your consideration.</b>

13:04.880 --> 13:10.040
<b>However, if you two plan on using demons
to inflict meaningless harm on people,</b>

13:10.630 --> 13:13.670
<b>then I will likely have to stand against you.</b>

13:15.290 --> 13:19.130
<b>I'll let you go for now, as per my master's wishes.</b>

13:19.130 --> 13:23.630
<b>But if you ever try to stand in Lord Yasuhide's way,
then I won't hold back.</b>

13:24.960 --> 13:27.080
<b>The same goes for me.</b>

13:38.790 --> 13:40.880
<b>This just seems to be an ordinary restaurant.</b>

13:41.420 --> 13:42.880
<b>What shall we do now?</b>

13:44.130 --> 13:48.460
<b>I think it's best we steal the Yatonomori Kaneomi
from Sugino-dono before another tragedy occurs.</b>

13:48.960 --> 13:51.290
<b>But we can't do that unless we find him first.</b>

13:51.790 --> 13:54.080
<b>Perhaps we should ask the staff here.</b>

13:55.170 --> 13:56.170
<b>Good idea.</b>

13:59.000 --> 14:01.710
<b>The bossman's slower than molasses gettin' here!</b>

14:02.040 --> 14:06.290
<b>Maybe he ain't comin' today? Whoa nelly!</b>

14:06.750 --> 14:07.830
<b>My apologies.</b>

14:08.040 --> 14:10.080
<b>Nah, it's me that's done bumped into you!</b>

14:11.920 --> 14:15.330
<b>Aw shucks. Let me treat ya
to a bit'o hooch for the trouble!</b>

14:15.500 --> 14:16.290
<b>Huh?</b>

14:16.580 --> 14:19.500
<b>The hand'o fate broutcha fellas here for a reason!</b>

14:19.750 --> 14:25.670
<b>Um, well, while we do appreciate your generosity,
we still have some business to attend to.</b>

14:26.040 --> 14:27.170
<b>Ya don't say?</b>

14:27.420 --> 14:30.540
<b>If you don't mind, may I ask you one thing?</b>

14:30.540 --> 14:31.250
<b>Shoot.</b>

14:31.790 --> 14:34.630
<b>Do you know a man by the name Mataroku Sugino?</b>

14:37.040 --> 14:38.460
<b>Nope, never heard of 'im!</b>

14:38.920 --> 14:42.330
<b>I see. Sorry for the odd question. Thank you.</b>

14:42.540 --> 14:45.000
<b>Pshaw, don't mention it.</b>

14:45.540 --> 14:46.540
<b>Catchya 'round!</b>

14:49.380 --> 14:53.380
<b>Hope nobody drank all my hooch while I was gone...</b>

14:53.380 --> 14:58.380
<b>He's a Tosa native. I wonder if he's
part of the group pushing for expulsion?</b>

15:00.040 --> 15:00.960
<b>Pardon me.</b>

15:00.960 --> 15:01.830
<b>Yes?</b>

15:02.080 --> 15:04.210
<b>Who are those men in the inner parlor?</b>

15:04.210 --> 15:07.000
<b>Oh, they're regulars here.</b>

15:07.000 --> 15:11.130
<b>A bunch of patriots trying to stand up
for the country or some such.</b>

15:11.130 --> 15:15.420
<b>They're always drinking while chatting
about big and complicated topics in there.</b>

15:17.080 --> 15:19.710
<b>Do you know this "bossman" they speak of?</b>

15:20.000 --> 15:23.670
<b>Sure. A "Takechi-sama..." if I remember right.</b>

15:23.960 --> 15:26.580
<b>He's a gentleman who they all seem to respect.</b>

15:30.420 --> 15:33.330
<b>Jin-dono. What were you trying to find out?</b>

15:33.330 --> 15:40.130
<b>I suspected that our man Sugino might have come to this
restaurant hoping to make contact with that group, but...</b>

15:40.750 --> 15:42.420
<b>it seems I was mistaken.</b>

15:42.790 --> 15:45.380
<b>Contacting the loyalists, eh?</b>

15:45.670 --> 15:48.080
<b>Unless he had a change of heart,</b>

15:48.080 --> 15:51.500
<b>Sugino-dono should side with the shogunate
given that he was serving Hatakeyama-dono.</b>

15:51.670 --> 15:56.080
<b>If anything, that would put him in opposition
to the imperialists who were drinking in there.</b>

15:56.880 --> 15:57.500
<b>Jin-dono.</b>

15:57.790 --> 16:01.500
<b>That man with the Tosa accent mentioned
their "bossman" hadn't shown up yet.</b>

16:02.670 --> 16:09.290
<b>I'm willing to bet plans were made for one of
the loyalist bigwigs to visit this restaurant soon.</b>

16:09.830 --> 16:14.130
<b>And if Sugino-dono caught wind of that,
then as a member of the opposition, he would...</b>

16:14.750 --> 16:16.580
<b>...try to sabotage it.</b>

16:17.290 --> 16:21.880
<b>What's more, if we consider the name that
Hatakeyama-dono dropped to be accurate,</b>

16:21.880 --> 16:23.670
<b>then this "bossman" is...</b>

16:25.960 --> 16:30.670
<b>...the founder of the Tosa Loyalist Party, Zuizan Takechi.</b>

16:31.750 --> 16:36.380
<b>Meaning that Mataroku Sugino is coming here
with plans to assassinate Zuizan Takechi?</b>

16:36.630 --> 16:42.330
<b>Hatakeyama-dono intentionally let that information
about Sugino slip, so that we would notice.</b>

16:42.710 --> 16:46.790
<b>And he likely had planned on recruiting you
since long before today, Jin-dono.</b>

16:47.500 --> 16:49.380
<b>That's exactly why he summoned for you.</b>

16:50.290 --> 16:52.670
<b>The cursed sword was just bait, huh?</b>

16:53.830 --> 16:57.380
<b>He wins big if Zuizan Takechi actually gets assassinated.</b>

16:57.790 --> 17:02.500
<b>But even should that fail, he's succeeded
at getting a chance to meet directly with you.</b>

17:03.000 --> 17:08.960
<b>That all suggests he foresaw Sugino
plotting an assassination. What a cutthroat man.</b>

17:09.580 --> 17:15.380
<b>The fact he's throwing his weight around like this
is proof the shogunate is heading for the rocks.</b>

17:15.710 --> 17:18.880
<b>It might already be too late for our government...</b>

17:23.040 --> 17:25.960
<b>I'm sorry. I didn't meant to get so emotional.</b>

17:26.750 --> 17:27.460
<b>It's okay.</b>

17:28.670 --> 17:30.290
<b>So, what should we do?</b>

17:30.750 --> 17:37.080
<b>If there's any chance that cursed sword is making
Sugino-dono bloodthirsty, then we can't leave him be.</b>

17:38.580 --> 17:40.710
<b>No, that's just a lofty excuse.</b>

17:40.710 --> 17:45.960
<b>This little scheme rubs me the wrong way
and I'll have work to do if the cursed sword is real.</b>

17:46.920 --> 17:48.750
<b>That's reason enough.</b>

17:52.790 --> 17:58.540
<b>This blade gives me all the power I need to slaughter
those braindead fools obsessed with the Emperor.</b>

18:01.830 --> 18:05.040
<b>Zuizan Takechi must also meet his end.</b>

18:05.040 --> 18:07.750
<b>Yeah. He deserves to die!</b>

18:09.330 --> 18:10.920
<b>I'll tell you upfront.</b>

18:11.960 --> 18:15.250
<b>I don't consider assassination to be cowardly.</b>

18:15.580 --> 18:18.250
<b>Katana are nothing but weapons, after all.</b>

18:19.210 --> 18:24.040
<b>It makes no different how they're used,
since killing is all they can do.</b>

18:24.420 --> 18:25.880
<b>Therefore, I don't spurn you.</b>

18:26.790 --> 18:27.630
<b>However...</b>

18:28.630 --> 18:31.460
<b>I'm sorry. I must put a stop to this.</b>

18:32.210 --> 18:34.500
<b>What? Who the hell are you?!</b>

18:41.420 --> 18:43.540
<b>His slash flew through the air?</b>

18:43.960 --> 18:46.330
<b>Now that's an interesting parlor trick.</b>

18:46.920 --> 18:48.540
<b>How are you still alive?</b>

18:48.540 --> 18:50.880
<b>Sorry, but I'm sturdier than your average man.</b>

18:51.080 --> 18:53.830
<b>Whatever! Then I'll turn you into mincemeat!</b>

18:53.830 --> 18:56.790
<b>I need this! Need to kill!</b>

18:59.750 --> 19:02.250
<b>You can't block with that dull piece of shit forever!</b>

19:31.250 --> 19:34.000
<b>A katana that's infused with demonic power, eh?</b>

19:41.210 --> 19:42.250
<b>Assimilation.</b>

19:52.250 --> 19:54.420
<b>Kaneomi. Are you done?</b>

19:54.420 --> 19:58.040
<b>Yeah. This is the blade I forged by using your blood.</b>

19:58.630 --> 20:02.040
<b>It turned out good. I think I'll forge about three more.</b>

20:02.580 --> 20:08.750
<b>I'll inscribe the long swords with the signature
"Yatonomori" and the short swords with "Kaneomi."</b>

20:09.330 --> 20:12.580
<b>But can they really harbor demonic power?</b>

20:12.880 --> 20:13.500
<b>I dunno.</b>

20:14.080 --> 20:16.040
<b>"Yatonomori" and "Kaneomi."</b>

20:16.290 --> 20:20.500
<b>I'm curious to know where these katana
that share our names will end up in 100 years.</b>

20:20.500 --> 20:23.250
<b>But unfortunately, I won't live that long.</b>

20:24.290 --> 20:28.170
<b>So, Yato, I want you to go and find out for me.</b>

20:29.580 --> 20:33.960
<b>If it turns out they do have special powers,
then don't let it shake your faith.</b>

20:34.500 --> 20:37.290
<b>Humans can be stupid and make mistakes at times.</b>

20:37.670 --> 20:41.420
<b>While demons can butt heads because
of how stubbornly they stick to their guns.</b>

20:41.750 --> 20:46.750
<b>But we live in the same world.
Demons and humans can coexist, ya know?</b>

20:47.670 --> 20:48.710
<b>All right.</b>

20:50.000 --> 20:53.000
<b>Sorry. I know that I'm asking a lot.</b>

20:53.000 --> 20:58.290
<b>Don't be. Helping my husband's dream come true
is all part of being a wife.</b>

21:19.960 --> 21:22.960
<b>"Demons and humans can coexist."</b>

21:34.830 --> 21:38.380
<b>So, Sugino-dono really
was making his way to that restaurant.</b>

21:39.130 --> 21:41.040
<b>What a bone-chilling story.</b>

21:41.250 --> 21:45.290
<b>To have his soul warped by a cursed blade
and forced to murder his own wife...</b>

21:45.830 --> 21:48.210
<b>No. That's not quite accurate.</b>

21:48.210 --> 21:48.920
<b>Huh?</b>

21:49.130 --> 21:52.630
<b>While it's true the Yatonomori Kaneomi
was a cursed blade,</b>

21:52.960 --> 21:56.380
<b>the special power it possessed was "skyedge."</b>

21:56.380 --> 22:00.000
<b>It unleashes flying slashes. And nothing more.</b>

22:00.330 --> 22:03.630
<b>O-okay, but then, why did Sugino-dono kill his wife?</b>

22:07.500 --> 22:09.960
<b>But why, darling...?</b>

22:10.250 --> 22:14.040
<b>N-no! I didn't! It's not me!</b>

22:14.290 --> 22:18.670
<b>Th-the sword! I only attacked you because of its curse!</b>

22:18.670 --> 22:19.670
<b>It's not my fault!</b>

22:19.670 --> 22:22.000
<b>Yeah. I'm not to blame.</b>

22:22.000 --> 22:26.380
<b>This sword makes anybody want to go
on a killing spree. That's just how it works!</b>

22:26.580 --> 22:28.710
<b>The sword is what killed you!</b>

22:28.710 --> 22:32.880
<b>Not me! It just took control of my mind!</b>

22:42.080 --> 22:46.460
<b>He slashed his wife merely because
she was within reach. That's all.</b>

22:47.380 --> 22:48.500
<b>My God...</b>

22:48.960 --> 22:54.000
<b>But he couldn't handle the truth, and thus
chose to believe the sword made him do it instead.</b>

22:54.460 --> 22:56.920
<b>That twisted side of him might be
what Hatakeyama hoped to exploit.</b>

22:57.750 --> 23:02.040
<b>Then, Sugino-dono wasn't going to assassinate
that man for the sake of the country at all.</b>

23:02.290 --> 23:06.670
<b>He was just looking for an excuse to kill someone
and Hatakeyama-dono gave it to him, is that right?</b>

23:07.580 --> 23:09.500
<b>It's hard to say what the truth is.</b>

23:15.790 --> 23:19.630
<b>I'm impressed you stood up to him
and refused to compromise on how you live.</b>

23:27.380 --> 23:31.750
<b>Now I think... It might be time for me
to settle on my own course in life.</b>
